      "wk-faq": {
        "type": "wk-faq",
        "settings": {
          "eyebrow": "Questions, answered",
          "heading": "The honest answers",
          "subhead": "No spin, no over-promising. If something isn't here, our team reads every message.",
          "q1": "I'm not sure I'm in perimenopause yet — is this for me?",
          "a1": "Most likely, yes. Perimenopause can begin in your early forties — often years before the word menopause feels like it belongs to you. If you're noticing changes in sleep, mood, bloating, or temperature and a doctor has told you your labs are \"normal,\" this formula was built for exactly that window.*",
          "q2": "Does it contain hormones?",
          "a2": "No. There is no estrogen, progesterone, or any hormone in this formula. It works through named botanicals, vitamins, and a probiotic blend that support your body's own systems — including the estrobolome — rather than adding hormones to them.*",
          "q3": "How is this different from a multivitamin or other menopause supplements?",
          "a3": "Most of the category hides behind proprietary blends and fairy-dust doses. We name and dose every active at the level the research actually used — 200mg ashwagandha, 100mg standardised black cohosh, 100mg red clover isoflavones, and a 10 billion CFU probiotic blend. You can read exactly what you're taking, and how much, on the panel.",
          "q4": "How do I take it?",
          "a4": "Two gummies daily, with or without food, at a time you'll remember — there's no loading phase and no routine to build your day around. Consistency matters more than timing, so pick a moment that sticks. Each bottle is 60 gummies, a full 30-day supply at the two-a-day serving.",
          "q5": "When will I notice a difference?",
          "a5": "Many women report steadier sleep and a calmer stress response within two to three weeks. Bloating and mood often follow by week four, with the fuller picture — cooler nights, steadier days — by weeks six to eight as the actives reach steady state. Consistency matters more than timing.*",
          "q6": "Can I take it alongside my medications or other supplements?",
          "a6": "Because every ingredient and dose is on the label, you and your clinician can review it in full. Some botanicals — black cohosh and chasteberry among them — can interact with certain medications or conditions, so please check with your healthcare provider before starting, especially if you are taking medication, are pregnant, or are nursing.",
          "q7": "Is it really sugar-free — and what does it taste like?",
          "a7": "Yes — no added sugar and no sugar alcohols that upset the gut. The gummy is a deep-red cranberry, lightly tart rather than candy-sweet, designed to be a daily you actually look forward to without working against the formula's gut support.",
          "q8": "What is the estrobolome, and why does it matter?",
          "a8": "It's the community of gut bacteria that helps metabolise estrogen. When it falls out of balance — as it often does in the transition — recirculating estrogen can swing, feeding bloating, mood shifts, and disrupted sleep. Our probiotic blend supports that gut–hormone conversation, so the rest of the formula has steadier ground to work on.*",
          "q9": "How does the subscription work, and what if it's not for me?",
          "a9": "Your subscription ships free on your chosen cadence, and you can pause, skip, or cancel anytime from your account — no emails, no hoops. And because the formula needs a full transition cycle to show what it can do, every order is backed by our 90-day money-back guarantee: take the whole three months, and if it isn't right for you, reach out for a full refund — no need to return the bottles.",
          "footer_text": "Still wondering about something?",
          "cta_label": "Ask our team",
          "cta_link": ""
        }
      },
